! R8: pp -> H2 H2 -> b b~ b b~, m_H2 = 150 GeV, physical ctau = 4.32622152973311191 mm.
! benchmark_id = H2scan_mH150_tb300000
!
! Production kinematics come from the CANONICAL physical MadGraph 3.5.3 LHE
! sample (g g > H > h2 h2, sqrt(s) = 13 TeV), materialized and merged in
! fbientrigo/dihiggs_hep_cross PR #10 (merge commit
! f601e318c57f780d21e8dbee4dcccd7ec1b7b88a):
!   run_01: artifacts/h2_first_physical/madgraph/run_01/unweighted_events.lhe.gz
!   sha256 = 1c580b7a590f9bbfbf213eeef0e54fdcc4b6c1dce3f13bc0ed5278f6f3aec202
! This is NOT the R7 simplified stand-in LHE
! (results/r7_h2_pair_4b/input/h2pair_m150_1000events.lhe.gz); its cross
! section must never be used for physical normalization.
!
! The LHE's stable final-state PDG has been relabelled 9000006 -> 35 (a pure
! text substitution of the LHE PDG code via scripts/relabel_lhe_pdg.py; mass,
! momenta and event kinematics are byte-identical -- verified: 2000 IDUP
! fields changed, 0 mismatches elsewhere). This reuses the same validated
! mechanism as cards/r7_h2_pair_4b/ctau_4p326mm.cmnd in the R7 recast
! (fbientrigo/dihiggs_llp_recast PR #5): Pythia8's ResonanceDecays machinery,
! needed to shower the b b~ decay products into real jets, requires a
! registered ResonanceWidths object that only exists for Pythia's own
! built-in resonance slots (e.g. PDG 35, "H0"); a fully custom PDG (9000006)
! has none.
!
! Shower configuration (FSR on, ISR on, MPI off, hadronization on, Tune:pp =
! 21) is reused unchanged from the R7 real-recast path: it is the config
! validated to process this same gg -> H -> h2h2 topology through the real
! DV+jets analysis, as opposed to the standalone hep_cross full-Pythia sample
! (ISR/FSR/MPI off), which validates lifetime/decay bookkeeping only and is
! not evidence for jet acceptance.
!
! The physical PDG 35 width (mWidth, printed by R7_LLP_SETTINGS below) is
! Pythia's default H0 width, NOT the physical H2 width
! (4.56118529862185007e-14 GeV per the hep_cross production manifest). It
! does not affect the generated lifetime because 35:tauCalc = off and tau0 is
! forced via Recast:llpTau0 below, but it is a real divergence between the
! simulated particle and the physical model point.
!
! Recast:llpPdgIds and the 35:... particle-data lines are placed before the
! Main:subrun block deliberately (see R7 card): the recast binary reads
! Recast:llpPdgIds immediately after pythia.readFile(), before init() runs.
!
! Random:seed is independent per run (Phase 4 requirement); R7's card set no
! seed at all (both R7 lifetime runs implicitly shared Pythia's default
! seed), which R8 must not repeat.
Main:numberOfEvents = 1000
Main:timesAllowErrors = 3
Init:showChangedSettings = on
Init:showChangedParticleData = off
Next:numberCount = 5000
Next:numberShowInfo = 0
Next:numberShowProcess = 0
Next:numberShowEvent = 0

Random:setSeed = on
Random:seed = 81001

PartonLevel:MPI = off
PartonLevel:ISR = on
PartonLevel:FSR = on
HadronLevel:Hadronize = on
Tune:pp = 21

Higgs:useBSM = on
35:m0 = 150.
35:mMin = 100.
35:tauCalc = off
35:tau0 = 4.32622152973311191
35:onMode = off
35:onIfMatch = 5 -5

Recast:llpPdgIds = {35}
Recast:llpTau0 = 4.32622152973311191
LesHouches:setLifetime = 2

Beams:frameType = 4
LHEFInputs:nSubruns = 1
Main:subrun = 0
Beams:LHEF = data/raw/r8_h2_model_derived_4b/relabelled_run_01.lhe.gz
